{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>Thus, with fire</b> — in its plain sense: to judge the world with fire, as in 'for by fire YHWH executes judgment' (Isaiah 66:16), or that the heat intensifies, as though it burns with fire and the latter rain does not fall." "<b>And it consumed the portion</b> — the portion of the field; this is a noun of species [collective], like 'and I had ox and donkey' (Genesis 32:6)."], :book :amos, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Amos -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/amos"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:18:26.366043316Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}